<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bophuthatswana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1977">1977</a>–<a href="/years/1994">1994</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bophuthatswana was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">Bantustan</a> created by apartheid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> for Tswana-speaking people, declared independent in 1977 but recognised by no country other than South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. It consisted of several separate enclaves, with its capital at Mmabatho, and was ruled by Lucas Mangope. After his overthrow in March 1994 it was reincorporated into South Africa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bophuthatswana.jpg" alt="Bophuthatswana" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Washiucho · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bophuthatswana_(1972%E2%80%931994).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
